diff --git a/go.work b/go.work
index 4685372..e9513ec 100644
--- a/go.work
+++ b/go.work
@@ -1,19 +1,21 @@
 // This repository contains two Go modules: github.com/spiffe/go-spiffe/v2 at the
 // root and the lightweight github.com/spiffe/go-spiffe/lite under lite/. The
-// workspace makes local builds and tests resolve lite from disk.
+// workspace makes in-repo builds and tests resolve lite from disk, so changes
+// that span both modules can be developed and tested together.
 //
-// Releasing is therefore two steps, lite first:
+// The root go.mod always requires a released lite tag and carries no `replace`
+// directive (replace-check enforces this). Consumers ignore `replace` in a
+// dependency's go.mod, so this keeps every tip of main resolvable for anyone
+// pinning the v2 module at a branch or commit, and it makes the GOWORK=off CI
+// build verify the resolution consumers actually see.
 //
-//  1. Tag the lite module:  lite/vX.Y.Z
-//  2. In the root go.mod, drop the `replace` directive and set the lite
-//     `require` to the version just tagged.
-//  3. Run `GOWORK=off go mod tidy` and confirm `GOWORK=off go build ./...`
-//     succeeds, which is how consumers resolve the dependency.
-//  4. Tag the v2 module:  vX.Y.Z
+// Releasing is two steps, lite first:
 //
-// The `replace` directive exists so the repository builds before lite has ever
-// been tagged. Consumers ignore `replace` directives in dependency go.mod files,
-// so the `require` line must point at a real tag by release time.
+//  1. Tag the lite module:  lite/vX.Y.Z
+//  2. If the release includes lite changes the v2 module needs, bump the lite
+//     `require` in the root go.mod to the new tag and run
+//     `GOWORK=off go mod tidy`.
+//  3. Tag the v2 module:  vX.Y.Z
 
 go 1.24.0
 
